From: Brian Ellis <brianellis@gotenna.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: u_serial: fix NULL deref in gs_close() after failed open

gs_open() can fail before assigning tty->driver_data, for example when
the port has been removed or allocating the write buffer fails. The TTY
core still calls ->close() to unwind the failed open. gs_close() then
dereferences the NULL port while taking port_lock.

Return without touching the port when the open did not claim it. Keep
the successful-open close path unchanged.

Backport of the proposed minimal fix; this does not address other port
lifetime races or establish why a particular open failed.

Fixes: c1dca562be8a ("usb gadget: split out serial core")
Link: https://lkml.rescloud.iu.edu/2610.1/13659.html
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c
@@ -695,6 +695,9 @@ static void gs_close(struct tty_struct *tty, struct file *file)
 	struct gs_port *port = tty->driver_data;
 	struct gserial	*gser;
 
+	if (!port)
+		return;
+
 	spin_lock_irq(&port->port_lock);
 
 	if (port->port.count != 1) {
